flowchart TB
  accTitle: Finite voltage descent and its stop conditions
  accDescr: Every accepted step lowers voltage. Floor, unsafe cache, ordinary failure and Balanced efficiency walls return a passing point; critical errors abort.
  INPUT([Start with a passing baseline or tier reference]) --> FLOOR["Choose the floor<br/>Explicit floor → model-table floor → fallback<br/>Unknown model: 10% below starting voltage"]
  FLOOR --> NEXT{"A lower editable bin remains<br/>at or above the effective floor?"}
  NEXT -->|No| RETURN([Return the selected passing curve])
  NEXT -->|Yes| BUILD["Build the complete next candidate<br/>Hold requested MHz; retain measured upward gains<br/>Use the same tail policy"]
  BUILD --> CACHE{"Actual new voltage/clock<br/>blocked by unsafe cache?"}
  CACHE -->|Yes| RETURN
  CACHE -->|No| PROBE["Apply through the daemon and probe<br/>Q2RTX + CUDA, telemetry and runtime guardrails"]
  PROBE --> RESULT{"Probe outcome"}
  RESULT -->|Critical| ABORT([Abort the whole run])
  RESULT -->|Ordinary failure| RETURN
  RESULT -->|Pass| ACCEPT["Record the passing evidence<br/>Update the latest safe point<br/>Persist accepted selections"]
  ACCEPT --> WALL{"Balanced: confirmed FPS/W wall<br/>after the required voltage drop?"}
  WALL -->|Yes: keep the better selected point| RETURN
  WALL -->|No / other tier| NEXT
  classDef work fill:#18382f,stroke:#80d9ac,color:#edf5fa,stroke-width:1.5px
  classDef gate fill:#302c20,stroke:#e9bd76,color:#fff0d8,stroke-width:1.5px
  classDef stop fill:#40252a,stroke:#ef9595,color:#fff0f0,stroke-width:1.5px
  class INPUT,FLOOR,BUILD,PROBE,ACCEPT,RETURN work
  class NEXT,CACHE,RESULT,WALL gate
  class ABORT stop
